! Oracle anchor, v1.20.0.  Single point at the EXACT geometry the
! reference program used -- taken from the ORCA input of the
! comparison run, not re-derived from the Z-matrix, so the two
! programs see the same molecule to the last digit.
!
! Settings follow the verification protocol of the StudDFT paper:
! spherical shells, grid 8 (Treutler-Ahlrichs M4) for DFT, tight
! SCF.  ORCA ran with Grid5 GridX5 IntAcc 6.0, TightSCF, NoRI,
! NoCOSX and SCF tolerances at 1e-10.
!
! Reference: HF
%method  HF
%basis   cc-pVDZ
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%spherical
%scf_etol 1e-10
%scf_ptol 1e-8
%scf_diis_etol 1e-7
%geom angstrom
H       0.0000000000      0.0000000000      0.0000000000
C       0.0000000000      0.0000000000      1.0900000000
H       1.0661808848      0.0000000000      1.3166237430
*end
